---
// Curated page for the Flexalighting North America application
// (Graphic Designer & Social Media Specialist). noindex.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Rawan Aladdin — for Flexalighting North America"
  description="Print, product literature and social media work by Rawan Aladdin, gathered for Flexalighting North America, with her contribution on each."
  noindex={true}
  bodyClass="fl-pitch"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/flexalighting.css" />
  </Fragment>
  <main class="fl-main">
    <section class="fl-hero">
      <hr class="fl-rule" />
      <p class="fl-label">For Flexalighting North America &#183; Graphic Designer &amp; Social Media Specialist</p>
      <h1>A brand, carried onto everything it lives on.</h1>
      <p>I&#8217;m Rawan Aladdin, a designer in Surrey. This page follows your posting: product literature and print first, then the social media work you asked to see, with my part in each spelled out. My resume and cover letter are <a href="/flexalighting/Rawan_Aladdin_Flexalighting.pdf">here as a PDF</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="fl-sec">
      <p class="fl-label">01 &#183; Print and product literature</p>
      <h2>Feeds: brand identity, guidelines and launch</h2>
      <p class="fl-meta">Freelance, 2026 &#183; client: an open-source developer tool</p>
      <p>I designed the Feeds identity and its eleven-page guidelines. These four pages are the ones a spec-sheet designer would look at first: logo usage with four explicit don&#8217;ts, a five-colour palette with a usage-ratio bar, a five-step type scale with each step named for its job, and fifteen icons that share one stroke, grid and join.</p>
      <ul class="fl-spec"><li>11 guideline pages</li><li>5-step type scale</li><li>15 custom icons</li><li>Usage ratios for every colour</li></ul>
      <div class="fl-grid4">
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/feeds/guidelines-05.webp" alt="Feeds guidelines, logo usage page with three approved lockups and four don'ts" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/feeds/guidelines-06.webp" alt="Feeds guidelines, colour palette page with a usage-ratio bar" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/feeds/guidelines-07.webp" alt="Feeds guidelines, typography page with a five-step type scale" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/feeds/guidelines-08.webp" alt="Feeds guidelines, iconography page with fifteen icons on one grid" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:22px">When the launch came, the same system went onto printed table runners, die-cut stickers in four colourways, two looping booth reels, the marketing site and the product&#8217;s email digest. The engine is the developer&#8217;s; everything you can see is mine.</p>
      <div class="fl-wide">
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/feeds/feeds-booth.webp" alt="The Feeds launch booth: two printed table runners, die-cut stickers, and the brand reel looping on screen" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="fl-sub">Surface Fixer: identity, print and templates</h3>
      <p class="fl-meta">Freelance, 2026 &#8211; present &#183; client: my family&#8217;s surface-repair business</p>
      <p>A wordmark where the X in &#8220;Fixer&#8221; is a crossed bandage, repeated out into a pattern. I designed the business cards and sent the print files to the printer myself, redesigned the website, and built an invoice and document template system in Google Docs and Sheets so the business can produce its own paperwork on-brand.</p>
      <div class="fl-wide">
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/surfacefixer-cover.webp" alt="Surface Fixer identity, the crossed-bandage mark replacing the X, over its pattern" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="fl-sub">Ancient Retrospect: a printed publication</h3>
      <p class="fl-meta">BCIT assignment, 2024 &#183; InDesign, printed</p>
      <p>A publication on the mosaics of the Hagia Sophia: a cover system, small-caps captions and full-bleed photographic spreads on one grid, taken all the way to print. It is the piece closest to what your literature asks for: long-form layout, image-led pages, and type that stays quiet beside photography.</p>
      <div class="fl-wide" style="max-width:420px">
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/playground-retrospect.webp" alt="Ancient Retrospect publication cover on the mosaics of the Hagia Sophia" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="fl-sec">
      <p class="fl-label">02 &#183; Social media, and what I did on each</p>
      <h2>SyriaTek: Instagram and Facebook</h2>
      <p class="fl-meta">Jun &#8211; Aug 2026 &#183; began as a BCIT term project, published as a public pilot &#183; <a href="https://www.instagram.com/syria.tek/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@syria.tek</a></p>
      <p>Your posting asks applicants to explain their contribution, so each project here is broken into the parts you named. SyriaTek is an Arabic-language technology series for Syrians at home and abroad, explained the way an older cousin would over coffee.</p>
      <dl class="fl-contrib">
        <dt>Design</dt><dd>Arabic and Latin wordmarks drawn to sit together, a chip mark, profile and Facebook cover versions, an animated wordmark, and two 1080&#215;1920 pilots cut in CapCut with Arabic subtitles and English stacked beneath.</dd>
        <dt>Copywriting</dt><dd>The Arabic scripts and captions. I used ChatGPT for first drafts and rewrote them by ear, because hearing what was wrong in Arabic was faster than starting the sentence myself.</dd>
        <dt>Content planning</dt><dd>A reusable production guide fixing the audience, the 30&#8211;45 second format, a four-part script structure, B-roll direction and quality checks.</dd>
        <dt>Account management</dt><dd>Published both pilots, read the analytics and reported the result honestly.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="fl-result">My sister filmed the street footage in Syria for me; I presented on camera, then selected, cut, captioned and exported. No visuals were AI-generated.</p>
      <p class="fl-result"><b>After 15 days:</b> 3,823 views and 1,556 unique viewers, with about 92% of views from people who did not follow the account. <b>And the miss:</b> my goal was 100 followers and I reached 21. Two introduction videos found an audience; a steady calendar of useful lessons is what would have kept it.</p>
      <div class="fl-ig-grid">
        <div class="fl-ig">
          <p class="fl-ig-k">Pilot one &#183; Welcome</p>
          <blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbNR4HenYQQ/?utm_source=ig_embed" data-instgrm-version="14">
            <div class="fl-ig-fallback">
              <img src="/syriatek/syriatek-frame-1.webp" alt="A frame from the SyriaTek Welcome pilot: the presenter on camera with Arabic and English subtitles stacked beneath." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="fl-ig-fb-body"><a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbNR4HenYQQ/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on Instagram &#8599;</a></div>
            </div>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
        <div class="fl-ig">
          <p class="fl-ig-k">Pilot two &#183; Digital Skills</p>
          <blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-permalink="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbPvv6KhE3K/?utm_source=ig_embed" data-instgrm-version="14">
            <div class="fl-ig-fallback">
              <img src="/syriatek/syriatek-broll-2.webp" alt="A street in Syria at dusk, B-roll used in the SyriaTek Digital Skills pilot." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="fl-ig-fb-body"><a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbPvv6KhE3K/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on Instagram &#8599;</a></div>
            </div>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fl-two">
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/syriatek/syriatek-cover.webp" alt="SyriaTek Facebook cover with the bilingual wordmark" loading="lazy" /></div>
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/syriatek/syriatek-timeline.webp" alt="The CapCut timeline for a SyriaTek pilot, with two caption tracks" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="fl-sub">Instagram for Ctrl. Alt. Defeat.</h3>
      <p class="fl-meta">BCIT coursework, MKTG 3010 Marketing in the Attention Economy &#183; <a href="https://www.instagram.com/ctrlaltdefeat_/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@ctrlaltdefeat_</a></p>
      <p>A team follower-growth competition. I took the lead on the account.</p>
      <dl class="fl-contrib">
        <dt>Design</dt><dd>Made the posts with my team.</dd>
        <dt>Content planning</dt><dd>Planned a professional shoot for the team.</dd>
        <dt>Account management</dt><dd>Set up the account and the team&#8217;s mission and ran it through the competition.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p class="fl-result"><b>Result:</b> 80 followers in a day and a half, and the team won.</p>

      <h3 class="fl-sub">South African Cultural Association of BC</h3>
      <p class="fl-meta">Internship, Jul &#8211; Sep 2023 &#183; Graphic Web Designer &amp; Project Manager</p>
      <dl class="fl-contrib">
        <dt>Design</dt><dd>Web and social graphics designed in Figma as one visual system with the new site.</dd>
        <dt>Content planning</dt><dd>Coordinated the social campaign for an upcoming event.</dd>
        <dt>Account management</dt><dd>Project manager for the team of six that redesigned the association&#8217;s website and social pages.</dd>
      </dl>
      <div class="fl-wide">
        <div class="fl-thumb"><img src="/sacabc-mockup-1.webp" alt="The redesigned SACABC website shown on screen" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="fl-sec">
      <p class="fl-label">03 &#183; Photography</p>
      <h2>A year behind the camera</h2>
      <p>For a year at the University of Toronto Muslim Students&#8217; Association I was the event photographer and the only editor, directing two to four volunteer shooters and finishing everything in Adobe Creative Cloud.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="fl-sec fl-honest">
      <h2>Plainly</h2>
      <p>I have not worked in CAD or 3D modelling, and I have not run an email marketing campaign; my email work so far is the Feeds digest design. I know Google Analytics and Meta Ads Manager from coursework. Working with your team in Italy would be new, and I would be glad to learn it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="fl-sec fl-about">
      <p class="fl-label">Contact</p>
      <p>Rawan Aladdin &#183; Surrey, BC &#183; available on site &#183; <a href="mailto:hello@rawanaladdin.com">hello@rawanaladdin.com</a> &#183; 778-239-8020 &#183; <a href="https://rawanaladdin.com">rawanaladdin.com</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script is:inline async src="https://www.instagram.com/embed.js"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var imgs = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.fl-thumb img'));
      if (!imgs.length) return;
      var lb = document.createElement('div');
      lb.className = 'fl-lb';
      lb.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
      lb.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
      lb.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Image viewer');
      lb.innerHTML =
        '<button class="fl-lb-close" type="button" aria-label="Close">×</button>' +
        '<button class="fl-lb-prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous image">‹</button>' +
        '<figure class="fl-lb-fig"><img alt=""><figcaption class="fl-lb-cap"></figcaption></figure>' +
        '<button class="fl-lb-next" type="button" aria-label="Next image">›</button>';
      document.body.appendChild(lb);
      var lbImg = lb.querySelector('img');
      var lbCap = lb.querySelector('.fl-lb-cap');
      var closeBtn = lb.querySelector('.fl-lb-close');
      var prevBtn = lb.querySelector('.fl-lb-prev');
      var nextBtn = lb.querySelector('.fl-lb-next');
      var main = document.querySelector('main');
      var idx = -1, lastTrigger = null, sb = 0, sd = 0;
      function order() { return [closeBtn, prevBtn, nextBtn]; }
      function show(i) {
        idx = (i + imgs.length) % imgs.length;
        var src = imgs[idx];
        lbImg.src = src.getAttribute('data-full') || src.currentSrc || src.src;
        lbImg.alt = src.alt || '';
        lbCap.textContent = src.alt || '';
      }
      function openLb(i, trigger) {
        lastTrigger = trigger || null;
        sb = document.body.scrollTop; sd = document.documentElement.scrollTop;
        show(i);
        lb.setAttribute('data-open', 'true');
        if (main) main.setAttribute('inert', '');
        document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        closeBtn.focus();
      }
      function closeLb() {
        lb.removeAttribute('data-open');
        if (main) main.removeAttribute('inert');
        document.body.style.overflow = '';
        document.body.scrollTop = sb; document.documentElement.scrollTop = sd;
        if (lastTrigger) lastTrigger.focus();
      }
      imgs.forEach(function (img, i) {
        var btn = document.createElement('button');
        btn.className = 'fl-zoom';
        btn.type = 'button';
        btn.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Open full size' + (img.alt ? ': ' + img.alt : ''));
        img.parentNode.insertBefore(btn, img);
        btn.appendChild(img);
        btn.addEventListener('click', function () { openLb(i, btn); });
      });
      closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeLb);
      prevBtn.addEventListener('click', function () { show(idx - 1); });
      nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function () { show(idx + 1); });
      lb.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === lb) closeLb(); });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (lb.getAttribute('data-open') !== 'true') return;
        if (e.key === 'Escape') { e.preventDefault(); closeLb(); }
        else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') { e.preventDefault(); show(idx - 1); }
        else if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') { e.preventDefault(); show(idx + 1); }
        else if (e.key === 'Tab') {
          var f = order(), first = f[0], last = f[f.length - 1];
          if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { e.preventDefault(); last.focus(); }
          else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) { e.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
